Subject: [PATCH 5/5] [M159] [PageInfo] Guard site data dialog WebContents

Original change's description:
> [PageInfo] Guard site data dialog WebContents
>
> When fixing the Contextual Tasks side panel Page Info site data dialog
> crash (crrev.com/c/8757191), `OnManageOnDeviceSiteDataClicked()` and
> `OnDialogExplicitlyClosed()` guarded `web_contents_` in case the
> underlying `WebContents` is destroyed while the modal dialog widget is
> still closing asynchronously. The remaining methods on
> `PageSpecificSiteDataDialogModelDelegate` still assumed `web_contents_`
> was non-null.
>
> Align `web_contents_` and `BrowsingDataModel` null checks across the
> remaining `PageSpecificSiteDataDialogModelDelegate` methods so all
> dialog callbacks and browsing data lookups return safely if the
> `WebContents` has been destroyed.
>
> Bug: 579921184
> Change-Id: Ia35e29ba33ad79f82e35c7a3ac4de46a65cd161c
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8758951
> Reviewed-by: Mike Wasserman <msw@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Duncan Mercer <mercerd@google.com>
